  "title": "Oikonomou2016 – SSVEP MAMEM 1 dataset",
  "description": "A dataset of 256-channel EEG recordings from 11 healthy adults performing an SSVEP-based brain-computer interface protocol. Participants viewed a single flickering box at five stimulation frequencies (6.66, 7.50, 8.57, 10.00 and 12.00 Hz) while signals were recorded with an EGI 300 Geodesic EEG System at 250 Hz. The data support comparative evaluation of SSVEP signal processing and classification algorithms.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with an EGI GES 300 amplifier and a 256-channel HydroCel Geodesic Sensor Net at 250 Hz. Each session included rest, an adaptation period, and 5-second flickering windows at each of five frequencies, with rest periods between windows. Stimuli were shown as a magenta flickering box on a 22-inch, 60 Hz LCD monitor.",
